mshtml: no readystate notification for a document object that is gone.

notif_readystate dereferences window->browser->doc, which is NULL once the
document object has let go of the browser. A queued load event can still reach
it then: the Digimon SuperRumble launcher (a WinForms web view on Wine Gecko,
playing an H.264 video) closes its window right after starting the game and
crashes in call_property_onchanged reading NULL->cp_container.

Riftway, offered under LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine.

--- a/dlls/mshtml/persist.c
+++ b/dlls/mshtml/persist.c
@@ -441,7 +441,9 @@
     if(frame_element)
         IHTMLDOMNode_AddRef(&frame_element->element.node.IHTMLDOMNode_iface);
 
-    if(is_main_content_window(window))
+    /* Riftway: a load event can arrive after the document object let go of the
+     * browser (a launcher closing its window right after starting a game). */
+    if(is_main_content_window(window) && window->browser->doc)
         call_property_onchanged(&window->browser->doc->cp_container, DISPID_READYSTATE);
 
     hres = create_document_event(inner_window->doc, EVENTID_READYSTATECHANGE, &event);
